Package: tidyvisor
Title: A Statistical Advisor for Research: Design, Analysis and Interpretation
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jimmy", "Moses", , "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3342-2384"))
Description: A chief statistician for R. Before the data are collected,
    'tidyvisor' advises on study design, the unit of replication, sample
    size (power analysis) and good research practice, with the reporting
    guideline for the field. Given data and a question, it audits the data,
    checks the assumptions of the candidate analyses and recommends the
    analysis, the test and the plots, with the code to run and what to do
    when assumptions fail. Given a fitted result, it explains the numbers in
    plain sentences, with its reasons, so the advice can be checked and
    overruled. Specialised knowledge lives in the packages that do the
    analyses, each of which registers an advisor: 'tidydiversity' for
    community ecology and 'tidymapr' for spatial ecology.
